%U A398474 476,484,525,544,568,588,633,647,688,706,737,760,811,827,868,892,927,953,1010,1021
%N A398474 a(n) is the number of sets of two or more pairwise coprime integers >= 2 whose product is at least n, but whose product divided by the smallest member is less than n.
%C A398474 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of minimal pairwise-coprime moduli sets for a residue number system covering {0,...,n-1}.
%C A398474 Every member of such a set is necessarily less than n, since the product excluding the smallest member must itself be less than n.
%H A398474 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="/A398474/b398474.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..10000</a>
%e A398474 a(6) = 5: the valid sets are {2,3}, {3,4}, {2,5}, {3,5}, {4,5}.
%Y A398474 Cf. A324837 (minimal subsets with LCM = n).
%K A398474 nonn
%O A398474 2,4
